# Exam track — Theme: De Stot — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
#
# These are the user's real answers, gathered by interview — do not "improve"
# or genericize them in a later editing pass. The point is that the learner
# rehearses what they will actually say in the Sproochentest.
#
# Question order follows the reported real exam: the examiner opened on the
# PARENTS' household (how long the candidate lived there, which chores were
# theirs versus their parents', whether they helped), then moved to the present
# household, the cleaning lady and why there is none, and how cleaning feels.
# That cluster is answered first and in the most depth.
#
# The @fill blocks carry frames that recur across any topic: well-causal,
# wann-conditional, obwuel-contrast, léiwer-wéi comparative, fir…ze purpose,
# dofir inversion, wärenddeems-temporal, a duration, a frequency adverb, a past
# participle, a number, and an Ech-mengen hedge.

@lesson W1.03 "Talking About Household Chores"

